Z||000047||Borgio||11-05-2001||09:08 PM||||I'm wondering why BlackStang95 was dissing FieroKyle. $3K isn't that much to spend. Insurance for a teenager can be very expensive. Mine is almost $100 a month. That is liability only. Sports car surcharge of 30%. Good student discount, 30%. This is about the average price for someone my age. Lots of people pay more. I don't know how long he has had his car for, but $100 times 30 months equals $3000. Plus gas and any minor repairs. I'm in college right now and I didn't bring my car to save on insurance. I wish I had, but thats beside the point. Cars cost money, insurance prices suck. ||||reg||1
